From 4e0dd19435ecb467a6dc55254387d06fd185e066 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Takuro Fukamizu <takuro.f.1987@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:57:21 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] h3game: add H3_BACKEND=server (h3-control-server) and
 frame_seq freshness
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

bridge.py
- H3_BACKEND=legacy|server|dry (default legacy: seat path unchanged; H3_DRY=1 still
  means dry and wins over server). H3_SERVER_URL defaults to
  http://127.0.0.1:8892.
- server: never imports h3_direct / serial. connect() only opens the
  transport to the control server (no ARM, START or centering); the 60 Hz
  USB resend, the 1 s fade to center and auto_sway are off; "auto" requests
  are ignored and counted (auto_ignored). do_POST hands the accepted body
  (pitch, roll, yaw, gain, frame_seq, frame_age_ms) to the backend without
  waiting on the network; an exception from the backend is logged and
  counted (backend_errors) and the POST still gets its answer. /state
  keeps its keys and adds backend, rig_state, armed, calibration_valid,
  fault, server_url, effective_gain, axis_conflict, hud_note and more.
  /reconnect re-opens the transport only. The /state poll never counts as
  game liveness.
- All modes: bind the HTTP port before connect(). A second launch on a busy
  port exits without touching the seat or the server (in server mode it
  used to take the server session first, which stopped the ride and locked
  out the running bridge).
- All modes: GET /reconnect and /claim from a non-loopback peer are ignored
  ({"ignored": true}), like the POSTs already were. Either one stopped the
  ride from any device on the LAN; the page opened from another PC is
  view-only anyway.

web/index.html
- Count completed rAF frames (frame_seq) and send frame_seq and frame_age_ms
  with every seat POST. frame_seq does not advance while the tab is hidden.
- While hidden the POST still carries zeros (legacy unchanged) but repeats
  the frame_seq last POSTed while visible (and that frame's age). rAF runs
  ahead of the 30 Hz POST, so sending the current frameSeq would pair zeros
  with a frame the server has not seen and drive the seat toward center.
- Server mode only (st.backend === "server"): the play HUD and the setup
  card add rig_state, a lost session, FAULT, the server's axis-assignment
  note (/state hud_note: 系統の競合 / 個体の不一致 / 再基準化が必要) and a
  capped gain to the connection text. /state "connected" is false once
  another client took the session, so the page no longer says "接続中" /
  "席 OK" while this bridge's poses go nowhere. Legacy pages look the same.

New files: h3_server_backend.py (adapter), h3_motion_client.py (copy of
the client from dof-reality-h3-custom-controller). Server mode needs
`pip install websockets` (>= 13). The backend does nothing about an
axis_conflict reject besides reporting it (poses keep flowing; the server
accepts them again once the operator fixes the CoreS3 selection).

